      "text": "To solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the function \\(f(x) = ax + b\\) given that \\(g(f(x)) = 3x + 4\\) and \\(g(x) = 2x - 5\\), we start by substituting \\(f(x)\\) into \\(g(x)\\).\n\nThe function \\(f(x)\\) is given by:\n\\[ f(x) = ax + b \\]\n\nThe function \\(g(x)\\) is given by:\n\\[ g(x) = 2x - 5 \\]\n\nWe need to find \\(g(f(x))\\):\n\\[ g(f(x)) = g(ax + b) \\]\n\nSubstitute \\(ax + b\\) into \\(g(x)\\):\n\\[ g(ax + b) = 2(ax + b) - 5 \\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\\[ g(ax + b) = 2ax + 2b - 5 \\]\n\nWe are given that:\n\\[ g(f(x)) = 3x + 4 \\]\n\nTherefore, we can set the expression equal to \\(3x + 4\\):\n\\[ 2ax + 2b - 5 = 3x + 4 \\]\n\nFor the equation to hold for all \\(x\\), the coefficients of \\(x\\) and the constant terms must be equal on both sides. Thus, we equate the coefficients of \\(x\\) and the constant terms separately:\n\\[ 2a = 3 \\]\n\\[ 2b - 5 = 4 \\]\n\nSolve the first equation for \\(a\\):\n\\[ 2a = 3 \\]\n\\[ a = \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\nSolve the second equation for \\(b\\):\n\\[ 2b - 5 = 4 \\]\n\\[ 2b = 9 \\]\n\\[ b = \\frac{9}{2} \\]\n\nNow, we find \\(a + b\\):\n\\[ a + b = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{9}{2} \\]\n\\[ a + b = \\frac{3 + 9}{2} \\]\n\\[ a + b = \\frac{12}{2} \\]\n\\[ a + b = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
